{
  "title": "Focalboard \u2014 Project Management / Productivity (26,169\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Focalboard\nDomain: Project Management / Productivity | Scale: medium | Stars: 26,169\nProblem: Provides an open-source, self-hosted alternative to commercial project management tools like Trello, Notion, and Asana. Enables teams and individuals to define, organize, track, and manage work without vendor lock-in.\nTarget users: Individual users (personal desktop app), Small to medium teams, Organizations seeking self-hosted solutions, Developers and technical teams\nCore features: Kanban boards with cards and columns; Multi-user collaboration and sharing; Task management and tracking; Cross-platform desktop apps (Windows, macOS, Linux); Personal server deployment for teams; REST API for integrations; Multilingual support\nIntegrations: Mattermost (plugin version available), Docker containerization, REST API endpoints for custom integrations\nTech stack: TypeScript, React, SCSS + Go + SQLite (desktop), configurable for server + Docker, Electron (desktop), WPF (.NET for Windows), macOS native, GTK (Linux)\nKey libraries: React, TypeScript, Go standard library, Electron, Docker\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Full-stack TypeScript/Go architecture enables code sharing and consistent tooling across frontend and backend\n- Multi-platform desktop distribution strategy (App Stores + direct downloads + Docker) maximizes accessibility\n- Modular build system (make-based) supports selective compilation for different targets (web, desktop variants)\n- Self-hosted emphasis with SQLite default reduces infrastructure requirements and privacy concerns compared to SaaS alternatives",
